  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SME Trade Finance Facility (STFF): Trade Finance and Investment Climate Support for SMEs in ACP countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The SME Trade Finance Facility (STFF) is a blended finance initiative to help address the significant SME trade finance gap in African, Caribbean and Pacific countries and reach small- and medium-sized importers and exporters who are `most in need&#xbf; and has been developed by UNCDF, together with the European Commission (EC) and the Organization of African Caribbean and Pacific States (OACPS). STFF aims to strengthen financial ecosystems and the investment climate for im/export-oriented SMEs in selected ACP countries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;The main objectives of STFF are to enable access, improve usage of new and existing trade finance products for SMEs, fostering trade openness, economic diversification and job creation in select ACP countries. Although trade finance serves as the lifeblood of international trade and SME engagement in trade is known to be an engine of growth, there are persistent financing and de-risking gaps in ACP countries which disproportionately impact SMEs and constrain their ability engage in trade and contribute to sustainable, inclusive economies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
